{
  "year": 2016,
  "pointsSystem": "Per-event placement points on CrossFit's 2016 Games table for a 40-athlete field. Events 2016-01 through 2016-10, 2016-14 and 2016-15 awarded a maximum of 100 points to the event winner; the three short Sunday-morning tests - Handstand Walk (2016-11), Suicide Sprint (2016-12) and The Plow (2016-13) - were worth a maximum of 50 points each (half value). Points descend with place (full-value events: 1st=100, 2nd=94, 3rd=88, 4th=84, 5th=80, 6th=76, 7th=72, 8th=68, 9th=64, 10th=60, then ~2 per place; the three half-value events use roughly half those figures). Tied placings share points (e.g. Fraser and Ben Smith both 505 lb / 34 pts at place 23 in the deadlift ladder). Each athlete's 15 event points sum to totalPoints; the theoretical maximum is 1,350. All places, scores and points are taken from the official CrossFit Games leaderboard archive (c3po.crossfit.com).",
